<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Deliberately empty, and that is the point: the helper needs no entitlement
	     to do its one job. It waits for a pid to exit and calls replaceItemAt on a
	     directory the app has already established it can write. Hardened runtime,
	     no App Sandbox, nothing else.

	     Applied by scripts/release.sh, which re-signs this binary WITH a secure
	     timestamp after the Developer ID export and before notarization. The app's
	     post-build script signs it with the timestamp suppressed, to keep Debug
	     builds offline and fast, and the notary service will not accept that.

	     Only ever handed to `codesign`, which accepts an empty dict; Xcode's own
	     build-time entitlements processing never sees this file.

	     Nothing in here may contain a doubled hyphen: it is an XML comment, so a
	     literal codesign flag written out breaks the file for AMFI's parser, and
	     the archive fails with "AMFIUnserializeXML: syntax error" naming a line
	     number and nothing else. -->
</dict>
</plist>
